Database commands are used to create, select, modify, and remove databases.

🟢 1. CREATE DATABASE

Creates a new database.

CREATE DATABASE company_db;
Safe version
CREATE DATABASE IF NOT EXISTS company_db;
🔵 2. USE DATABASE

Selects a database so that subsequent commands operate within it.

USE company_db;

⚠️ USE is supported by systems such as MySQL and SQL Server, but database selection syntax varies across SQL platforms.

🟡 3. ALTER DATABASE

Modifies database-level properties.

ALTER DATABASE company_db
MODIFY NAME = company_database;

⚠️ ALTER DATABASE syntax is database-specific. MySQL, SQL Server, PostgreSQL, and Oracle use different approaches for many database-level changes.

🔴 4. DROP DATABASE

Permanently removes a database and its objects.

DROP DATABASE company_db;
Safe version
DROP DATABASE IF EXISTS company_db;

🚨 Warning: Dropping a database removes the database structure and the objects/data contained within it.

